#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# algebraics

#% text
# `algebraics` is the domain of the algebraic numbers, the roots of nonzero polynomials with rational coefficients, for `element(x, algebraics)`.

#% section
# Details

#% item
# Rationals, `im` and their sums, products and rational powers are algebraic, and so are sin, cos and tan of rational multiples of pi.

#% item
# Not algebraic: `pi` and `e`; exp, log, sin, cos and tan at algebraic arguments other than 0 (log: other than 0 and 1) by the Lindemann-Weierstrass theorem; `b^c` for algebraic b other than 0 and 1 and algebraic irrational c by the Gelfond-Schneider theorem; a sum or product with exactly one transcendental part.

#% item
# Numbers outside these classes, such as `euler_gamma`, stay undecided.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
element((6 + im*sqrt(5))^(1/3), algebraics)
#% output
#= true

#% cell
element(pi, algebraics)
#% output
#= false

#% cell
element(sqrt(2)^sqrt(2), algebraics)
#% output
#= false

#% cell
element(sin(pi/7), algebraics)
#% output
#= true

#% cell
element(euler_gamma, algebraics)
#% output
#= element(euler_gamma, algebraics)

#% section
# See also

#% text
